# ============================================================
# ct-safety packaging exclusions for ClawHub publish.
# Mirror of .gitignore. The ClawHub packager uses this file to
# decide what to strip from the published package. Goal: never
# ship an openFDA API key or runtime caches/outputs.
# ============================================================

# ---- Secrets / API keys (NEVER ship) ----
.env
*.env
.env.*
*.key
*.secret
*.token
secrets.json
credentials.json
config.local.json

# ---- Runtime caches / downloaded outputs (not part of the skill) ----
out/
out_live/
*.cache
faers_summary_cache.json
faers_*.json
faers_*.csv
faers_*.xlsx
cn_pv.json
*.jsonl

# ---- Python cruft ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- Dev-only test harness (NOT shipped to ANY publish target) ----
# Per ct-base §16.8 (docs/07-publish-checklist.md L126-127): test source AND
# fixtures must not ship to ANY target — GitHub, ClawHub, or SkillHub.
# `tests/` is untracked (removed from the git index on 2026-08-31; the files
# remain on local disk for regression runs, but `git add -A --dry-run` stays
# clean). Both `.gitignore` and `.clawhubignore` list `tests/` so neither the
# GitHub tree nor the ClawHub package picks it up.
#
# Rationale: `tests/` uses importlib.util.exec_module / __import__ to discover
# and load test modules — ClawHub's static scanner flags this as
# `suspicious.dynamic_code_execution` (a false positive: it is stdlib module
# loading, not arbitrary-code execution). Stripping the directory keeps the
# published runtime surface clean.
#
# NOTE (2026-08-31): this block previously claimed ".gitignore intentionally
# keeps tests so the repo remains auditable" — that contradicted §16.8 and has
# been corrected. Auditability is preserved on local disk, not in the package.
tests/
tests/**

